<title>GERMANY: E.German Dec industry output rises 4.5 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>E.German Dec industry output rises 4.5 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Dec 96     Nov 96	 Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)  +4.5	 unch(-0.3)   -6.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		    +11.8	 +0.5(+0.1)    n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     147.0	140.7(140.2) 131.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. Previously reported data in brackets.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Dec 96		  Nov 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   160.2	+3.3     155.1	 +1.6</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    185.3	-0.1     185.5	 +0.7</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   128.8	-3.2     133.0	 +6.2</p>
<p> Energy output	     83.9	+2.7	81.7	 -4.6</p>
<p> Construction	     220.0	+7.3     205.1	 -0.3</p>
<p>Two month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Sept/Oct 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +1.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Nov/Dec 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +4.5</p>
<p> Mining				     -16.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		   +8.1</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	+10.7</p>
<p>		Capital goods		+2.9</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	 -10.4</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	    +13.6</p>
<p> Energy output			     -8.3</p>
<p> Construction				+5.2</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn Newsroom, 49-28-26097150</p>
</text>
